Automation Example: Gmail Processing


Psuedocode

Every 5 minutes: Get all unread emails sent to payment-ops@column.com
For each email:

Check if already created a case for this email thread
If no case exists:

Extract information from email
Detect priority (check for “urgent” keywords)
Detect case type (wire, ACH, etc.)
Get customer name and email
Get email subject and body

Create new case with extracted information
Mark email as processed (add label, mark as read)
Send notification to team via Slack

End


Code
function processInboundEmails() {
  // searches for unprocessed payment ops emails
  const query = 'to:payment-ops@column.com is:unread';
  const threads = GmailApp.search(query, 0, 50);

  threads.forEach(thread =&gt; {
    const firstMessage = thread.getMessages()[0];
    const threadId = thread.getId();

    // checks if case already exists
    if (!caseExistsForThread(threadId)) {
      // extracting info 
      const caseData = {
        priority: detectPriority(firstMessage.getSubject()),
        caseType: detectType(firstMessage.getSubject()),
        customerName: firstMessage.getFrom()
          .split('&lt;')[0].trim(),
        customerEmail: extractEmail(
          firstMessage.getFrom()),
        subject: firstMessage.getSubject(),
        description: firstMessage.getPlainBody()
          .substring(0, 500),
        gmailThreadId: threadId
      };

      const caseId = createNewCase(caseData);

      // label email, mark as read
      thread.addLabel(GmailApp
        .getUserLabelByName('Payment Ops Cases'));
      thread.markRead();
    }
  });
}
